# Prettier must not touch the documentation pages.
#
# It corrupts them, silently and in two distinct ways:
#
#  1. Inline code inside a JSX element is reformatted as if it were a JS
#     expression, so `${item/title}` in a <Note> comes back as `${item / title}` —
#     wrong text, shipped to the reader, no error anywhere.
#
#  2. Code fences are reformatted by the embedded formatter. It "fixed" an
#     `html` fence that deliberately showed an unclosed tag by closing it and
#     relocating the explanatory comment *inside* the element, inverting what the
#     example was demonstrating.
#
# Both are exactly the class of failure this package's own docs are about: a
# successful run that quietly produces the wrong output. Prose formatting is not
# worth it.
src/app/**/*.mdx

# Build output and vendored files.
.next/
out/
package-lock.json
